3]}],"hints":["Slow and fast pointers: when the fast one falls off the end, the slow one is in the middle."],"paramTypes":["list"],"returnType":"list","complexity":"O(n) time, O(1) space","starter":{"python":"# head is a ListNode built for you; the class is already defined.\n# Return a ListNode - it is serialised back for you.\ndef middleNode(head):\n    # TODO: implement\n    pass\n","javascript":"/**\n * @param {ListNode} head\n * @return {ListNode}\n */\nvar middleNode = function (head) {\n  // TODO: implement\n};\n"},"editorial":{"explanation":"Slow and fast pointers: the fast one moves two steps for every one the slow one takes, so when it\nfalls off the end, the slow one is halfway.\n\nLooping while `fast and fast.next` returns the **second** middle for even lengths, which is what\nthis problem asks for; looping while `fast.next and fast.next.next` returns the first.\n\n`O(n)` time, `O(1)` space, one pass — no length count needed.","code":{"python":"def middleNode(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow = slow.next\n        fast = fast.next.next\n    return slow\n"},"complexity":"O(n) time, O(1) space"}}
